# {{ .Name }}

{{ .Description }}

{{ template "chart.versionBadge" . }}{{ template "chart.typeBadge" . }}{{ template "chart.appVersionBadge" . }}

## Overview

{{ .Name }} consists of the following components:

- **Core**: init, document consumer, scheduler, optional Apache Tika and Gotenberg
- **WebServer**: Web UI
- **Worker**: Processes background jobs with celery
- **Database**: PostgreSQL for persistent storage
- **Broker**: A Dragonfly broker for work dispatch

Note: All the components can be configured for replicas except for core

## Prerequisites

- Kubernetes 1.19+
- Helm 3.0+
- A StorageClass, or existing PVCs
- A secure secret key

PostgreSQL and Dragonfly are bundled by default. Both can be disabled in favor of external services.

> [!WARNING]
> SQLite is supported for minimal installations, but requires the data persistent volume across workloads. It is **strongly discouraged** for production or multi-replica environments due to database
locking and lack of high availability.

## Installation

Add the Helm repository:

```bash
helm repo add myrepo https://charts.example.com
helm repo update
```

Install the chart:

```bash
helm install my-release myrepo/{{ .Name }}
```

## Configuration

The following table lists the configurable parameters and their default values.

{{ template "chart.valuesTable" . }}

## Examples

### Basic Installation

```bash
helm install my-app myrepo/{{ .Name }}
```

### Custom Configuration

```bash
helm install my-app myrepo/{{ .Name }} \
  --set replicaCount=3 \
  --set image.tag=v1.2.3 \
  --set ingress.enabled=true
```

### Using a Values File

Create a custom values file:

```yaml
replicaCount: 3

image:
  repository: myapp/app
  tag: v1.2.3

ingress:
  enabled: true
  className: nginx
  hosts:
    - host: myapp.example.com
      paths:
        - path: /
          pathType: Prefix
  tls:
    - secretName: myapp-tls
      hosts:
        - myapp.example.com
```

Install with custom values:

```bash
helm install my-app myrepo/{{ .Name }} -f custom-values.yaml
```

## Upgrading

```bash
helm upgrade my-app myrepo/{{ .Name }} --version {{ .Version }}
```

## Uninstalling

```bash
helm uninstall my-app
```

